// Exact match only, in both directions. `Sq` satisfies `Shape`, but a
// function taking a `Sq` does not satisfy a method taking a `Shape`: there
// is no contravariance, for the same reason interface satisfaction has
// none -- satisfaction is structural with no runtime coercion, and a
// variance rule would need the conversion the design does not have.
interface Shape { int sides(); }
type Sq {}
int Sq.sides() { return 4; }
interface Take { void take(Shape s); }
void take_sq(Sq s) { print(s.sides()); }
Take t = take_sq;
t.take(Sq());
